  m_Text: "Terms of Service\n\nWelcome to Water Bottle Sort Quest (the \"App\" or \"Service\"), operated by Ayooh Infotech (\"Company\", \"we\", \"our\", or \"us\").\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"Terms\") govern your access to and use of the Service. By downloading, installing, accessing, or using the App, you agree to comply with and be legally bound by these Terms. If you do not agree with any part of these Terms, please discontinue use of the Service.\n\nChanges to These Terms\n\nWe may revise or update these Terms from time to time to reflect changes in our services, legal requirements, or business practices.\n\nAny revised Terms will become effective when posted within the App or through other appropriate channels. Your continued use of the Service after any updates are published constitutes your acceptance of the revised Terms.\n\nEligibility\n\nTo use the Service, you represent and warrant that:\n\nYou are at least 13 years of age.\nYou satisfy the minimum age requirements applicable in your country or region.\nYou have the legal capacity to enter into a binding agreement.\nIf you are under the age of majority in your jurisdiction, your parent or legal guardian has reviewed and accepted these Terms on your behalf.\nYou are not prohibited from using the Service under applicable laws or regulations.\nYour access to the Service has not previously been permanently terminated by us.\nLimited License\n\nSubject to your compliance with these Terms, we grant you a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and revocable license to use the App solely for personal entertainment purposes.\n\nThis license does not transfer ownership of any rights related to the Service.\n\nRestrictions on Use\n\nUnless expressly authorized by us in writing, you may not:\n\nCopy, reproduce, distribute, publish, or commercially exploit any part of the Service.\nModify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works based on the App.\nReverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to discover the source code of the Service.\nUse the Service to develop competing products or services.\nRent, lease, sublicense, or transfer your rights to use the Service.\nProhibited Activities\n\nWhen using the Service, you agree not to:\n\nViolate any applicable law, regulation, or third-party right.\nAttempt to gain unauthorized access to systems, servers, or networks associated with the App.\nInterfere with or disrupt the operation, security, or performance of the Service.\nIntroduce viruses, malware, automated scripts, bots, or other harmful technologies.\nCollect information from the Service through automated means without permission.\nEngage in fraudulent, deceptive, abusive, or exploitative behavior.\nUse the Service in any manner that could damage our reputation or business operations.\n\nWe reserve the right to investigate and take appropriate action against any user who violates these Terms.\n\nIntellectual Property\n\nAll content, software, graphics, logos, trademarks, designs, and other materials contained within the Service are owned by us or our licensors and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.\n\nExcept as expressly permitted by these Terms, no rights are granted to users regarding such materials.\n\nService Availability\n\nWe strive to provide a reliable experience; however, we do not guarantee that the Service will always be available, uninterrupted, secure, or error-free.\n\nThe Service may occasionally be unavailable due to maintenance, upgrades, technical issues, or circumstances beyond our control.\n\nUpdates and Modifications\n\nWe may at any time:\n\nAdd, remove, or modify features and functionality.\nRelease updates, patches, or new versions.\nSuspend, restrict, or discontinue all or part of the Service.\n\nSuch actions may occur with or without prior notice.\n\nWe are not liable for any consequences arising from modifications, interruptions, or discontinuation of the Service.\n\nThird-Party Content and Links\n\nThe App may contain links to websites, advertisements, products, or services operated by third parties.\n\nWe do not own, control, endorse, or assume responsibility for third-party content or services. Your interactions with third parties are solely between you and the applicable provider.\n\nWe encourage you to review their terms, policies, and privacy practices before using such services.\n\nDisclaimer of Warranties\n\nThe Service is provided on an \"AS IS\" and \"AS AVAILABLE\" basis.\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, whether express, implied, statutory, or otherwise, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, and uninterrupted operation.\n\nWe do not guarantee that the Service will meet your expectations or be free from defects, errors, or security vulnerabilities.\n\nLimitation of Liability\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by law, Ayooh Infotech shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special, exemplary, or punitive damages arising from or related to your use of the Service.\n\nYour use of the Service is at your own risk.\n\nTermination\n\nWe reserve the right to suspend, restrict, or terminate your access to the Service at any time if we reasonably believe that you have violated these Terms or engaged in conduct harmful to the Service or other users.\n\nUpon termination, all rights granted to you under these Terms will immediately cease.\n\nGoverning Law\n\nThese Terms shall be governed and interpreted in accordance with applicable laws, without regard to conflict of law principles.\n\nContact Us\n\nIf you have any questions, comments, or concerns regarding these Terms of Service, please contact us at:\n\nEmail: natus.nasus5@gmail.com\n"
